{"key":"apphycem-mcq-006","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"The field component E_x is zero there.","working":"In electrostatics, the electric field component along x is E_x = -dV/dx. Since the point has a stationary potential, dV/dx = 0, so E_x = -0 = 0. Thus the field component must be zero. The value of V need not be zero; a stationary point can occur at any potential. Infinite charge and nonzero field are not required and are generally false.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":444,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":188,"cacheReadTokens":256},"outputTokens":286,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":123,"reasoningTokens":163},"totalTokens":730,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":444,"completion_tokens":286,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":256,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":188,"total_tokens":730,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":256},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":163}},"reasoningTokens":163,"cachedInputTokens":256},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3620,"keyed_label":"A"}
