{"key":"apphycem-mcq-027","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"kq/r","working":"The electric potential V(r) of a point charge q relative to infinity is given by V(r) - V(∞) = -∫_{∞}^{r} E · dr. Since the electric field of a point charge is E = (kq/r^2) r̂, integrating from infinity to r yields V(r) = -∫_{∞}^{r} (kq/r'^2) dr' = [kq/r']_{∞}^{r} = kq/r. Thus, with V(∞) = 0, the potential is V(r) = kq/r.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":352,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":352,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":332,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":163,"reasoningTokens":169},"totalTokens":684,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":169,"promptTokenCount":352,"candidatesTokenCount":163,"totalTokenCount":684,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":352}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":163}]},"reasoningTokens":169,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":2886,"keyed_label":"A"}
